  "limitations": [
    "Remediation record: docs/planning/reviews/C07/remediation-attempt-01.md (R1 cached attempts bound to Academy's lease and lock and re-read on reconnect; R2 offline store work in reset's write ledger; R3/R4 the latest unconfirmed lab work kept through one ordered device queue with confirmed clears; R5 serialized store commits, per-write temporary files, update() for revalidation, bounded and counted set-asides; R6 assembly byte budget; E1 contract-valid native parts; E2 the interrupted-write test in the common --lib command).",
    "Academy changes are on the owner-approved branch v2/desktop-presentation: commits 6c333b46, 9f24d67c and its test follow-up (after the C06 pin 7e8dcc79), pinned with tree hash in docs/architecture/inputs.lock.json, adds the LearnerHost localDrafts capability (LocalDrafts/LocalDraft types) and keeps unconfirmed desktop lab work on the device in use-desktop-draft.ts (the latest unconfirmed work kept after each edit, a failed save and on leaving the lab through one ordered queue; restored as 'saved on this device only', never sent by itself, forgotten once Academy holds the latest work, a failed clear asked again). Academy web regressions: docs/planning/evidence/C07/academy-regression.log (re-run at 9f24d67c) plus the xtask shared gates. The Academy branch is committed locally but not yet pushed: its husky pre-push hook's content suite keeps failing with vitest 'Timeout calling onTaskUpdate' RPC errors; the hook was not bypassed.",
    "D031 (decisions.md) and the DESIGN C07 section record the sealed store (chacha20poly1305 0.10.1 XChaCha20-Poly1305, per-account digest directory and lazily created deterministic Keychain key record), offline answer rules, revalidation without replay, localDrafts, locking, reset and Core::shutdown on RunEvent::Exit. Requirement matrix: docs/planning/evidence/C07/offline-matrix.md. Redacted storage manifest: docs/planning/evidence/C07/storage-manifest.json.",
    "Offline is a stopped synthetic endpoint natively (connections refused) and, in the Rust suite, a server that closes every request (token renewal included). Hosted Academy's offline contract (desktop.access/bundle/manifest/unitBundle) is qualified in C25 (L13); the synthetic endpoint (tools/native-acceptance/academy_server.py with academy_offline.py) follows Academy's router shapes at the pinned commit.",
    "The 512 MiB account budget and 1024-record cap are proven by the store unit test an_account_is_bounded_in_bytes_and_records (the record cap through the store, the byte budget at its boundary via within_budget); natively a course past the 16 MiB record limit is refused. Keychain denial and corrupt records are covered by the Rust offline suite, not natively.",
    "Native acceptance found a launch crash in the fixture host (offline work opened while installing the transport policy off the async runtime); fixed by opening only a new generation there (Core::start opens the restored one on the runtime) and guarded by the harness installing the policy off the runtime on every restart. It also found that the Downloads page stopped asking for the course list while unreachable, so Academy's return was never observed there; the page now re-asks every 15 s while unreachable.",
    "C01, C04, C05 and C06 native acceptance were re-run as regressions on the C07 bundle (docs/planning/evidence/C07/native-acceptance-C0x.json and native-regressions/); all pass on the remediated bundle (on the pre-remediation bundle C01-N06 once failed on one empty heading read and passed on rerun). The C06 driver expects, for builds after C06, the Downloads navigation entry and (C06-N08) the account's offline key remaining after sign-out with its locked work (the draft hook keeps unconfirmed lab work on the Mac after each edit, which creates the key; the refresh token is still revoked and removed; reset removes the key).",
    "Mutation probes: docs/planning/evidence/C07/mutation-probes (35 mutations across the core, store, write ledger, cached-attempt authority, revalidation races, assembly budget, Downloads page, snapshot contract, host adapter and Academy draft hook; baselines pass; run in a disposable copy)."
